The other night while wasting time trolling around the internet, I came 
across the story of an ascension in which the player ascended a healer 
who was wishless, foodless, pacifist, and had a bunch of other conducts 
as well.  While I considered this ascension to be absolutely impressive 
and worthy of great note, it required incredible patience and took over 
300,000 turns of game play to accomplish.

Personally, I just don't play that way. I'd rather have a 40,000 turn 
ascension with 1 conduct that takes two days than a 300,000 turn 
ascension with 8 conducts that takes months (and apparently the game I 
noted took a long time). I'd also rather I do it my way than Marvin's 
way, because that is the way I play.

Do I have weaknesses in my play? Sure. I tend to dump pets after getting 
strong enough, for instance (unless I have an insanely strong pet, but 
given my disregard for pets it rarely happens). As a consequence, I have 
never wished for a blessed figurine of an Archon, believe it or not. I 
tend to play marathon games for hours on end instead of saving 
cautiously and coming back to them. And I never use the E word.

But with 5 ascensions I do not consider myself a weak player, and I 
think the consensus is that anyone with just one ascension cannot be 
considered weak.

So if Marvin wants to use the E word he is welcome to it. I would not 
say he is weak for doing so, or even suggest it. But if it became public 
that Marvin's secret was that he ate Raisin Bran while playing, I 
wouldn't take this up because Marvin plays the way he plays and I play 
the way I play.

Just a thought.

